SUMMARY:Between Two Rivers: 250 Years of Pharmacy in Philadelphia
DESCRIPTION:Sitting between the Delaware and Schuylkill rivers\, Philadelph
 ia has long been a nexus of medicine-making traditions. The two freshwater
  rivers sustained life\, provided potable water\, and facilitated transpor
 tation and trade. The rivers were thus vital to the city’s rapid growth 
 in industry and government—a convergence that would enable Philadelphia 
 to become the birthplace of American pharmacy. \n\nHealing traditions and 
 household remedies were practiced and shared among Philadelphia’s…\n\n
 https://www.creativephl.org/arts-event/between-two-rivers-250-years-of-pha
 rmacy-in-philadelphia/
